{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1524318-why-is-vtm-so-allergic-to-a-character-being-an-inventor-visonary","id":1524318,"title":"Why is VTM so allergic to a character being an inventor/visonary?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-10-20T07:13:28-07:00","id":1524318,"title":"Why is VTM so allergic to a character being an inventor/visonary?","content":"I believe someone in the past mentioned here that inventor/visonary character builds don't see much use due to the ST's not wanting any change to the setting, and after playing for a while, that feeling seems to be somewhat common. My question is, why? As long as you are not going too crazy and making nuclear weapons or spaceships in the early 1900's, I don't see why it would be that large of an issue. I have also noticed that at times ST's will refrence real life science when talking about how it is unlikely for characters to make certain innovations.<br /> <br /> Which doesn't really make much sense to me. There are characters which are breaking the laws of nature using magic and disciplines, comparatively, what some of my characters were doing was much more tame. Plus, if someone has 5 in tech and computers, why can't they make robots somewhat similar to those found in cyberpunk 2077? From what I remember, having 5 in an ability makes you a vissonary in that field, and in STEM, there's always some advancement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-20T07:24:01-07:00","id":1524319,"title":"","content":"How does creating robots serve the themes of masquerade?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4270-literatzi","name":"literatzi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4270_2.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-20T07:34:20-07:00","id":1524320,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>literatzi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1524318-why-is-vtm-so-allergic-to-a-character-being-an-inventor-visonary?p=1524319#post1524319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does creating robots serve the themes of masquerade?</div> </div> </div> </div>Scouts for sect warfare. Perhaps drones would be a better word.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-20T07:42:08-07:00","id":1524321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1524318-why-is-vtm-so-allergic-to-a-character-being-an-inventor-visonary?p=1524320#post1524320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Scouts for sect warfare. Perhaps drones would be a better word.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe they meant the theme of the game. VtM isn't a sci-fi game, it isn't about space ships and journies to the moon in the early 1900s. It's a dark mirror of our reality. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Plus, if someone has 5 in tech and computers, why can't they make robots somewhat similar to those found in cyberpunk 2077? From what I remember, having 5 in an ability makes you a vissonary in that field, and in STEM, there's always some advancement. </div> </div> </div>Because there are plenty of people in our world who would have 5 in those skills and we don't have those things. Just because you're a visionary doesn't mean you get to have technology 50+ years ahead of what is available to everyone else. <br /> <br /> It sounds like you made a character that was, fundamentally, at odds with the setting and are upset it didn't work. That's understandable, your storyteller should have talked with you and let you know that your character idea didn't work before it came to the table. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9},{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-20T08:18:52-07:00","id":1524323,"title":"","content":"The game doesn't really support that because while you're supposed to <i>want</i> to make changes and improve things, you're not actually supposed to be able to <i>do</i> that. As such, the main driver behind whether or not something can be done isn't so much logic as it is &quot;mood&quot;, and so the game and STs tend to take arguments from each side of the spectrum depending on how they need to head the matter off at the pass. The conclusion is that vampires (or at least player characters) make things worse and can't change the world in any meaningful way, especially for the better. The supporting arguments change as needed.<br /> <br /> &quot;Why can't I create synthetic blood for vamps so they don't have to feed?&quot;<br /> &quot;Well, it's scientifically impossible so we're going to cleave to &quot;realism&quot; and rule that you can't do it.&quot;<br /> &quot;Well, if we're looking at realism, how can vampires do magic with their blood? How can we heal with our blood?&quot;<br /> &quot;Hey, it's just a game, not a realism simulator.&quot;<br /> &quot;OK, well, can I use that magical vampire blood to cure people of terminal diseases? Seems like we could make a pretty good organization of humans willing to donate blood if we can show that we can process that blood into anti-cancer juice.&quot;<br /> &quot;Uhh...*checking notes*&quot;<br /> <br /> (These kinds of arguments get really fun when you start asking if you can replicate feats known to be possible for vamps in-universe, like making your own Road/Path or developing your own Combo Disciplines)<br /> <br /> That said, early VtM 1 was somewhat about these things. Vampire Louis Pasteur was killed via political machinations specifically because he was an innovator as you describe - he canonically made a serum first to turn humans to vamps, then one to turn vamps into humans. Before the game began to solidify itself as Blood Weeping Simulator, it was quite willing to explore a multitude of themes. Early WoD was absolutely willing to get gonzo, and it's in that environment that your character might thrive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27305-joanna_crone","name":"Joanna_Crone","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-20T12:05:18-07:00","id":1524331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1524318-why-is-vtm-so-allergic-to-a-character-being-an-inventor-visonary?p=1524321#post1524321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I believe they meant the theme of the game. VtM isn't a sci-fi game, it isn't about space ships and journies to the moon in the early 1900s. It's a dark mirror of our reality.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, it could be a sci-fi crossover game. V:tR had a section in a general CoD book on it, and most of what applies to V:tR could easily be adapted to V:tM. The most important thing to preserve a lot of the mechanics would probably be to have vampires still hiding from humans but in space, but you could also have a throwback to V:tDA where they were more... open about things.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Because there are plenty of people in our world who would have 5 in those skills and we don't have those things. Just because you're a visionary doesn't mean you get to have technology 50+ years ahead of what is available to everyone else.<br /> <br /> It sounds like you made a character that was, fundamentally, at odds with the setting and are upset it didn't work. That's understandable, your storyteller should have talked with you and let you know that your character idea didn't work before it came to the table. </div> </div> </div>If you go by Mage, the Cam has actually purchased old models of HIT Marks (possibly for the most hilarious surprise to dump on shovelheads and their tenders when the Sabbat invades). So, really, it depends on the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-20T12:13:21-07:00","id":1524333,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1524318-why-is-vtm-so-allergic-to-a-character-being-an-inventor-visonary?p=1524331#post1524331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, it could be a sci-fi crossover game.</div> </div> </div> </div>It could be, but it doesn't sound like it was. If 3 players and a storyteller sit down for a gothic horror game and 1 person sits down for a space based sci-fi someone is having a bad time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you go by Mage, the Cam has actually purchased old models of HIT Marks (possibly for the most hilarious surprise to dump on shovelheads and their tenders when the Sabbat invades). So, really, it depends on the game. </div> </div> </div>I agree, it depends on the game. Such as Vampire being an entirely separate game from Mage, for example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-20T12:34:57-07:00","id":1524334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1524318-why-is-vtm-so-allergic-to-a-character-being-an-inventor-visonary?p=1524321#post1524321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because there are plenty of people in our world who would have 5 in those skills and we don't have those things. Just because you're a visionary doesn't mean you get to have technology 50+ years ahead of what is available to everyone else.</div> </div> </div> </div>I completely agree with this. A character with Computer, Science or Technology 5 will be acknowledged as an industry leader in those fields, but it shouldn't allow the character to have access to any technology that does not already exist. It just means your the equivalent of one the top researchers at Boston Dynamics, HPE, Lockheed Martin, etc. Anything that is actually &quot;super science&quot; is best left to Mage and the Technocracy in terms of the World of Darkness. Certainly anything that can be found in a future sci-fi setting like Cyberpunk 2077, but not in the real world, should not be allowed in a VtM chronicle.<br /> <br /> Certainly even if the character is capable of conceiving future technology, that does not mean the technical knowledge, industrial base, and manufacturing expertise actually exists to build it. Steve Jobs could drive the creation of the iPhone in 2007. He couldn't do it in 1983 when the best he could was the Apple Lisa. Vannevar Bush conceived the idea of a memex in the 1930s. But the fundamentals of the world wide web were not built until 1980s and did not become commercially available until the 1990s. AT&amp;T had functional videophone technology by 1970, but it wasn't commercially practical for many reasons. We wouldn't see actual video conferencing/communication technology until the 2000s when improvements in digital technology, infrastructure, and production cost made it actually feasible.<br /> <br /> Now of course many existing cutting edge technologies might give some capabilities that are hard for STs to understand how to incorporate into the game. STs can only handle so much of the unknown, and if a Player is pushing the ST to allow them to get away with something that is too disruptive, I think it's fine for the ST to say &quot;no&quot;. No matter how much more the players may know than the STs about a certain field, it is the ST's responsibility to run the game. In the context of the game's setting, the ST is the expert of what can be done, not the player. They can't allow any players to hijack the setting to allow something they want. If that is unsatisfying to the player, then that is something that must be negotiated to find a sweet spot everyone can live with.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-20T12:39:46-07:00","id":1524335,"title":"","content":"The theme of VtM is that of hopelessness, of grim darkness, of the corrosion of the soul due to the environment. At best you are a monster hanging on to its humanity, at worst you are a monster who has decided to find new levels of being a monster. Every problem is on a scale that it is impossible for you to do anything about it, other than perhaps survive long enough to see the next problem arrive.<br /> <br /> To be an inventor or a visionary is to inherently look at the situation and say &quot;I can change that&quot;. So already on a thematic and emotional level, being a creative character is at odds with the themes of the baseline game. Now there are plenty of creative vampire artist concepts but contrary to some people's beliefs, art by itself doesn't change anything. It may inspire or give emotional solace to another, but a masterwork sculpture or painting won't create jobs, cure a disease, or allow a war to be won.<br /> <br /> Now there is also the concept that an ST would have to map out all the changes to the setting due to a character inventing something. Invent the VtM equivalent of True Blood and practically the entire setting needs to be rewritten and every culture on the planet has to be modelled dealing with the vampires coming out of the coffin. Invent a new computer app and you have then model how all of that interacts with the online environment.<br /> <br /> This issue of having to rewrite the entire setting due to hypothetical advances is part of the reason why in many Isesaki anime/manga, the main character only &quot;invents&quot; things from our own world rather than creating new things, the writers can just look at our history to see how the technology affected the world. It's a lot of work to please just one character.<br /> <br /> It really comes down to the difference between simulation and story. An inventor wants to see their ideas interact with the world, thus a simulation. Alternatively, a character who made a new formulation for a type of makeup doesn't care about how the market share adjusts, they just use that as an explanation for why they have Resources 5 and a degree of Fame &amp; Influence in their Backgrounds.<br /> <br /> Of course, this is all going on before the subject of game balance comes up. Even if you don't invent a single thing and only apply real world technologies or concepts to the setting, the game balance implodes. For example, let us say that your character has Resources 5 and a science/inventor flavor. Now your ST has to figure out if the <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=0rB6L6AsBT8\" target=\"_blank\">3D printed titainium iron man suit</a> that is more or less immune to small arms fire can withstand werewolf claws. If it can't, the character concept is pointless, if it works then the entire power dynamic between shifters and vampires has changed because unlike trying to outfit an entire mortal army with these things, outfitting say 100 vampires with inherent fortitude (layered protection) and potence (to move the suit without a power source) is entirely viable.<br /> <br /> Hell, the game has yet to really address how the Tremere who have the Path of Technomancy, which makes them hackers second only technological mages, have not ended up running everything since they would literally be able to control anything connected to any form of internet. They even have a ritual that automatically causes all records of a location to be lost, misplaced, or otherwise deleted. This works for an entire year and can be reapplied so that the protection never lapses. Yet somehow V5 decided that Tremere chantries could be located and targeted by missile strike. The missiles use maps and GPS to hit the target as well as when to arm the warhead, the ritual would make the missile not know where the location was, thus it would just fly off or in circles until it ran out of fuel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-20T13:27:50-07:00","id":1524337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1524318-why-is-vtm-so-allergic-to-a-character-being-an-inventor-visonary?p=1524335#post1524335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The theme of VtM is that of hopelessness, of grim darkness, of the corrosion of the soul due to the environment. At best you are a monster hanging on to its humanity, at worst you are a monster who has decided to find new levels of being a monster. Every problem is on a scale that it is impossible for you to do anything about it, other than perhaps survive long enough to see the next problem arrive.<br /> <br /> To be an inventor or a visionary is to inherently look at the situation and say &quot;I can change that&quot;. So already on a thematic and emotional level, being a creative character is at odds with the themes of the baseline game. Now there are plenty of creative vampire artist concepts but contrary to some people's beliefs, art by itself doesn't change anything. It may inspire or give emotional solace to another, but a masterwork sculpture or painting won't create jobs, cure a disease, or allow a war to be won.<br /> <br /> Now there is also the concept that an ST would have to map out all the changes to the setting due to a character inventing something. Invent the VtM equivalent of True Blood and practically the entire setting needs to be rewritten and every culture on the planet has to be modelled dealing with the vampires coming out of the coffin. Invent a new computer app and you have then model how all of that interacts with the online environment.<br /> <br /> This issue of having to rewrite the entire setting due to hypothetical advances is part of the reason why in many Isesaki anime/manga, the main character only &quot;invents&quot; things from our own world rather than creating new things, the writers can just look at our history to see how the technology affected the world. It's a lot of work to please just one character.<br /> <br /> It really comes down to the difference between simulation and story. An inventor wants to see their ideas interact with the world, thus a simulation. Alternatively, a character who made a new formulation for a type of makeup doesn't care about how the market share adjusts, they just use that as an explanation for why they have Resources 5 and a degree of Fame &amp; Influence in their Backgrounds.<br /> <br /> Of course, this is all going on before the subject of game balance comes up. Even if you don't invent a single thing and only apply real world technologies or concepts to the setting, the game balance implodes. For example, let us say that your character has Resources 5 and a science/inventor flavor. Now your ST has to figure out if the <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=0rB6L6AsBT8\" target=\"_blank\">3D printed titainium iron man suit</a> that is more or less immune to small arms fire can withstand werewolf claws. If it can't, the character concept is pointless, if it works then the entire power dynamic between shifters and vampires has changed because unlike trying to outfit an entire mortal army with these things, outfitting say 100 vampires with inherent fortitude (layered protection) and potence (to move the suit without a power source) is entirely viable.<br /> <br /> Hell, the game has yet to really address how the Tremere who have the Path of Technomancy, which makes them hackers second only technological mages, have not ended up running everything since they would literally be able to control anything connected to any form of internet. They even have a ritual that automatically causes all records of a location to be lost, misplaced, or otherwise deleted. This works for an entire year and can be reapplied so that the protection never lapses. Yet somehow V5 decided that Tremere chantries could be located and targeted by missile strike. The missiles use maps and GPS to hit the target as well as when to arm the warhead, the ritual would make the missile not know where the location was, thus it would just fly off or in circles until it ran out of fuel.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, try and use technological solutions against Garou. See what happens.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-20T17:29:27-07:00","id":1524339,"title":"","content":"Well, vampires tend to be very creative outside of hard sciences. Brujahs are masters in politic upheavals, Lasombra can literally communicate with the darkness between the stars, Tremere, well, they were Mages and didn't forget that, Tzimisce can mold flesh and bone in creations both astounding and horrifying, Cappadocians &amp; Cia understand the death more than anyone else, etc. Sometimes what you need is not a titanium armor with a silver inlay and arabesques of gold and cold iron. What you need is a very charismatic businessman that would convince the people that these groves are places of crime and debauchery, and would be better cut down to put a new [insert some charity here]. So, yeah, there is space to inventions. Not the Technocratic ones, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27825,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27825-mrdrika","user":"MrDrika","date":". 10-20-2023, 08:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27825-mrdrika","name":"MrDrika","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27825_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-20T18:54:46-07:00","id":1524342,"title":"","content":"Probably it's a Gothic Horror game and if you're inventing shit, you're not exactly suffering for your dreadful curse of immortality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-20T19:00:07-07:00","id":1524343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1524318-why-is-vtm-so-allergic-to-a-character-being-an-inventor-visonary?p=1524342#post1524342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Probably it's a Gothic Horror game and if you're inventing shit, you're not exactly suffering for your dreadful curse of immortality.</div> </div> </div> </div>But gothic horror and strange inventions are kind of like chocolate and peanut butter. Strange inventions get created, and Victorian sensibilities can't help but get a case of the vapors and lament that man has gone too far, strayed into god's domain, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-20T19:22:58-07:00","id":1524345,"title":"","content":"Because vampires are undead, and often lack the certain spiritual/psychological spark that the living enjoy. In addition, the presence of the Beast will ultimately warp and twist anything the Damned try to do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-20T19:37:53-07:00","id":1524347,"title":"","content":"In general I'd steer clear of those ideas in a VtM game, but if someone wanted to explore making spaceships or robots or whatever, I'd be happy to run a Mage game where those ideas would be right at home. In general a hard sci-fi aesthetic simply doesn't really fit VtM and there are other, better games to explore those concepts. You'll have one player making death rays, robots and space ships and the rest of the group playing the night-to-night survival and personal horror that is VtM. The sci-fi player is going to be really breaking the mood of the game for the other players - the campaign could end up feeling a little bit like A Connecticut Yankee in King Arthur's Court.<br /> <br /> You risk having that one player twist or warp the game around their character, or at least have their character constantly breaking the mood of the game, and it ends up making it hard for the other players to enjoy the game. And at the end of the day, VtM is a group game and it's important that one player's enjoyment doesn't come at the expense of the enjoyment of everyone else. <br /> <br /> That said, if it was a solo game I wouldn't have an issue with that. Likewise, if someone was playing a Tremere or Tzimsci or such, and was using blood sorcery, homunculai or Viscissitude to create twisted robot-people hybrid monstrosities, then yeah I might be down because that at least hits the horror aspect of VtM. But it still risks seriously pushing the game in a non-traditional direction, so I'd want the other players to be on board with that before allowing that sort of thing to happen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-21T06:31:54-07:00","id":1524352,"title":"","content":"I think I should have been more clear, the whole spaceship thing was an example of something crazy that would be more than reasonable to be barred from doing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-21T09:24:31-07:00","id":1524355,"title":"","content":"We've had kindred who tried to be more then what they were and it always ended badly such as Michael and his lovers making Constaniople a paradise or the Brujah with Cathage, or the Ventrue, Lasombra &amp; Malkavians with Rome. Their jealous natures always undoes such efforts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-21T10:03:49-07:00","id":1524358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1524318-why-is-vtm-so-allergic-to-a-character-being-an-inventor-visonary?p=1524342#post1524342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Probably it's a Gothic Horror game and if you're inventing shit, you're not exactly suffering for your dreadful curse of immortality.</div> </div> </div> </div>To play a game of VtM, you are supposed to suffer from the curse of immortality. But if your character is going to survive long enough to establish themselves or perhaps become an elder, they by definition have to be adaptable enough and mentally capable enough to not be affected by the issues of being an immortal.<br /> <br /> Given enough time, the majority of the vampiric population would skew towards having these mental and emotional traits, due to attrition more than anything else. Which in turn means vampiric society as whole would in theory value those aspects. Thus a larger and larger percentage of childer would be selected for long term survivability first, and their mortal skills &amp; resources second.<br /> <br /> To put it another way, using the MBTI method for classifying people, most vampire elders behave similarly to INTJ type people due to storyline requirements. Theoretically this behavior pattern is learned over centuries of fighting to survive in an unforgiving environment. But after a certain point, you just start looking for potential embraces that are already INTJ classified mortals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-21T10:26:39-07:00","id":1524360,"title":"","content":"Like the others said, I think it's mostly a thematic concern. Building a clunky steam automaton in the 1900s? Sure! A remote controlled flying spy drone? Nah.<br /> <br /> Tinkerers are also notorious for inevitably meandering towards key inventions that straight up break the technology level of the setting, but I don't think that is something specific to Vampire. Almost every D&amp;D DM will have had that one player who wanted to discover nuclear fission or something. Vampire as a setting has maybe the extra caveat that vampires tend to be very static, traditional creatures. You have ancient laws and rules, rigid social structures- I mean, even their bodies reset back to default every evening.<br /> <br /> From an IC perspective, there is also the lack of motivation to invest time and resources if you can simply duplicate the benefits of an invention with a supernatural power. Why would I even think about inventing spy drones if I can just use Auspex or Animalism or Obfuscate or any number of magic rituals for the same benefit? Why build a robot if I can just animate a statue?<br /> The only advantage of replicating magic effects with mundane means is that you can sell your inventions to mortals and bolster your Resources, but even that gets problematic if those inventions are indistinguishable from actual magic to the wider public, or simply too good as to not draw attention.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-21T12:11:46-07:00","id":1524362,"title":"","content":"There is a True Brujah merit, called <b>Advanced Tech</b> (1-5 pt. Merit) [Lore of Bloodline p. 99]<br /> You have a device (or possibly a few) of an advanced design. While the True Brujah are not especially good at innovation, they are good at making improvements. So this device has no special functions unavailable to its contemporaries, but it does work a lot better. It reduces the chance of a mechanical fault (such as a jam) by half and all uses of the device are made with a -1 to the difficulty. The Storyteller should decide on the cost of the Merit, depending on how many items the character has, and how powerful they are.<br /> <br /> To reflect what the narrator True Brujah says about technology and science:<br /> <br /> &quot;<i>We are not just collectors of lore, but also students of it. With the vast resources at our command, we stand on the shoulders of giants when it comes to scientific advancement. While it is too dangerous to share the fruits of our labor with other Kindred or the kine, we do release some advancements into kine society when we need humanity to catch up.<br /> Now you would think that any scientist, given eternity and the best resources, would be able to change the world, cure cancer, develop true artificial intelligence, and more. Unfortunately, it has proved not to be the case. While our scientists are both dedicated and extremely intelligent, they are not innovators.<br /> It seems that the spark of creation and inspiration turns to ash when we become Kindred. It is a problem that haunts many of our most academic elders.<br /> That is not to say we waste our time, though.<br /> While we rarely innovate, we are very, very good at making improvements.<br /> Our technology does little that is new, but works much better and faster than its modern counterpart. This can often be an advantage, as it makes it easy to hide among less advanced equipment. For instance, our computers are simply faster than those available to humanity, even if they are not intelligent or organic</i>.&quot;\u200b<br /> <br /> It is nicely summarize this whole discussion<br /> Even with <i>literally all the time of the world </i>a vampire only manage to impove, but not <i>really</i> innovate","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-24T13:52:00-07:00","id":1524486,"title":"","content":"At Hello it should be noted is that the Kindred don't have all that much power over mortal society and have to exist in the shadows for safety as they know that if humanity truly became aware of them. It would be game over for the children of Caine as humanity has the tech and numbers to counter the powers of beings like Dracon, Mithras, Montano, Helena or Dracula.<br /> <br /> If any Kindred says that they rule a city that has over a million people is lying at best or is become very arrogant and believes there own hype and would be removed by more &quot;sane&quot; members of society. They can't take a front and center role in anything and can only encourage or take advantage of social, political and technological trends that humans create.<br /> <br /> Plus visionaries and innovators are somewhat uncommon irl and amongst the kindred more so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-24T22:34:56-07:00","id":1524498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1524318-why-is-vtm-so-allergic-to-a-character-being-an-inventor-visonary?p=1524486#post1524486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Plus visionaries and innovators are somewhat uncommon irl and amongst the kindred more so.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Toreador would be the best example for this actually, who - ironically - are the closest to Humanity<br /> Mozart's Embrace was catastrophic<br /> Fran\u00e7ois Villon? The Embrace had disastrous effects on him, he then lost this &quot;spark&quot; that the artists have. Sinking into a deep depression unable to continue her work, Helena abandoned him to his fate.\u200b<br /> Anna Yusupova? She became known as the \u201cSongbird of St. Petersburg.\u201d For a time, publications spoke of her as the Russian Mozart, saying her music could unite the nation. With the assassination of Tsar Alexander, it became clear this would not be. No matter how talented she was, she could not sing away the reality in her country. But after her Embrace, even as member of the Nephilim\u200b Toreador &quot;cult&quot; basically nothing remained of her mortal talent<br /> <br /> Even if you had that special &quot;umph&quot; as a Mortal, it fades after the Embrace if not completly dissapear...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-25T06:31:32-07:00","id":1524501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1524318-why-is-vtm-so-allergic-to-a-character-being-an-inventor-visonary?p=1524362#post1524362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is a True Brujah merit, called <b>Advanced Tech</b> (1-5 pt. Merit) [Lore of Bloodline p. 99]<br /> You have a device (or possibly a few) of an advanced design. While the True Brujah are not especially good at innovation, they are good at making improvements. So this device has no special functions unavailable to its contemporaries, but it does work a lot better. It reduces the chance of a mechanical fault (such as a jam) by half and all uses of the device are made with a -1 to the difficulty. The Storyteller should decide on the cost of the Merit, depending on how many items the character has, and how powerful they are.<br /> <br /> To reflect what the narrator True Brujah says about technology and science:<br /> <br /> &quot;<i>We are not just collectors of lore, but also students of it. With the vast resources at our command, we stand on the shoulders of giants when it comes to scientific advancement. While it is too dangerous to share the fruits of our labor with other Kindred or the kine, we do release some advancements into kine society when we need humanity to catch up.<br /> Now you would think that any scientist, given eternity and the best resources, would be able to change the world, cure cancer, develop true artificial intelligence, and more. Unfortunately, it has proved not to be the case. While our scientists are both dedicated and extremely intelligent, they are not innovators.<br /> It seems that the spark of creation and inspiration turns to ash when we become Kindred. It is a problem that haunts many of our most academic elders.<br /> That is not to say we waste our time, though.<br /> While we rarely innovate, we are very, very good at making improvements.<br /> Our technology does little that is new, but works much better and faster than its modern counterpart. This can often be an advantage, as it makes it easy to hide among less advanced equipment. For instance, our computers are simply faster than those available to humanity, even if they are not intelligent or organic</i>.&quot;\u200b<br /> <br /> It is nicely summarize this whole discussion<br /> Even with <i>literally all the time of the world </i>a vampire only manage to impove, but not <i>really</i> innovate</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> To be fair, that passage made me roll my eyes in disbelief. <br /> <br /> The extra diegetic reason for it is evident, the writers don't want the rational vampires to have futurist tech. <br /> But it is contradicted by everything we see in vtm. Vampires can be innovative, the very concept of creating thaumaturgical paths and rituals proves it. Vampires also invented philosophies, religion, etc<br /> <br /> It even contradict the kyasid chapter in the same book, whose main drive is creation, be it modification of their nature, new philosophies and so on. <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-25T10:34:07-07:00","id":1524504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1524318-why-is-vtm-so-allergic-to-a-character-being-an-inventor-visonary?p=1524501#post1524501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampires can be innovative, the very concept of creating thaumaturgical paths and rituals proves it.<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Do they really creating?<br /> Or re-create, copy something they had as humans either Mages or shamans, priests, etc...?<br /> Every Thaumaturgical, Koldunic, Necromantic, Voudoun etc Path and Ritual had a Human equivalent down the line...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1524318-why-is-vtm-so-allergic-to-a-character-being-an-inventor-visonary?p=1524501#post1524501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampires also invented philosophies, religion, etc<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, those philosophies and relegions are/were modified versions of pre-existing beief systems and relegions if we look them closely<br /> As much as the vampires love to bang their chest how &quot;inhumane&quot; those Paths are, most IF not all ofthem are actually quite... understandable from human point of view and you can find a human cult or sect or even a whole relegion that mirrored it or was very similar<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1524318-why-is-vtm-so-allergic-to-a-character-being-an-inventor-visonary?p=1524501#post1524501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It even contradict the kyasid chapter in the same book, whose main drive is creation, be it modification of their nature, new philosophies and so on.<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Well the Kiasyd are a bit more than vampires... (or less, depending of the point of view).<br /> That Fae blood is literal link to <i>dreams</i> and <i>imagination</i>\u200b and some even regulars in Changeling/Fae courts and treared as distant relatives (mostly by the Shadow Court and Unseelie society, true, but still... )<br /> <b>Bartholomew</b>\u200b is a good example of this; true, the '93 Storytellers Handbook to the Sabbat where he was intorduced is from an era, when crossovers were encouraged, but still, he was never retconned thus this pacifist 6th generation Inconnu children of Marconius is on good relations with the local Garou and Fae communities to he point there is a pack of werewolves called the Sunstringers who protect Bartholomew\u2019s haven and consider him one of the few Kindred deserving of an existence and Bartholomew have a team of Goblins who will aid him as much as they can...<br /> <b>The Arcadian</b>'s name speak for itself I think<br /> <b>B\u00e9atrice L'Angou</b> from Montreal by Night on the other hand is a scholar, collector of knowledge, but <i>not</i> an innovator and the Path of Nocturnal Redemption (a Path of Enlightenment created by the members of the coven known as the Shepherds of Caine) she follows is a potent mixture of human faith and Cainite enlightenment BUT builds on the Cainite'S faith as a mortal, there is nothing new in it basically or revolutionary. Just a modified version something that already existed and was important to someone.<br /> <br /> Wouldn't say the Kiasyd are a 'good' representatives of the Vampire race and limitations, considering they are with one foot is in another setting<br /> Kiasyd Alchemy is a strange mixology with very weird effects and backgrounds\u200b\u200b<br /> All and all, okay, I give you that, the Kiasyd could (and should) be an exeption but you must admit, they are the wierdest breed you could find in the setting (or settings)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-25T10:36:49-07:00","id":1524505,"title":"","content":"Soo...<br /> The flag system not liked my post<br /> The usual...<br /> Still HATE it with burning passion and my the Lords of Yomi feast on the soul whi designed this!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1524318-why-is-vtm-so-allergic-to-a-character-being-an-inventor-visonary?p=1524501#post1524501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampires can be innovative, the very concept of creating thaumaturgical paths and rituals proves it.<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Do they really creating?<br /> Or re-create, copy something they had as humans either Mages or shamans, priests, etc...?<br /> Every Thaumaturgical, Koldunic, Necromantic, Voudoun etc Path and Ritual had a Human equivalent down the line...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1524318-why-is-vtm-so-allergic-to-a-character-being-an-inventor-visonary?p=1524501#post1524501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampires also invented philosophies, religion, etc<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, those philosophies and relegions are/were modified versions of pre-existing beief systems and relegions if we look them closely<br /> As much as the vampires love to bang their chest how &quot;inhumane&quot; those Paths are, most IF not all ofthem are actually quite... understandable from human point of view and you can find a human cult or sect or even a whole relegion that mirrored it or was very similar<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1524318-why-is-vtm-so-allergic-to-a-character-being-an-inventor-visonary?p=1524501#post1524501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It even contradict the kyasid chapter in the same book, whose main drive is creation, be it modification of their nature, new philosophies and so on.<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Well the Kiasyd are a bit more than vampires... (or less, depending of the point of view).<br /> That Fae blood is literal link to <i>dreams</i> and <i>imagination</i>\u200b and some even regulars in Changeling/Fae courts and treared as distant relatives (mostly by the Shadow Court and Unseelie society, true, but still... )<br /> <b>Bartholomew</b>\u200b is a good example of this; true, the '93 Storytellers Handbook to the Sabbat where he was intorduced is from an era, when crossovers were encouraged, but still, he was never retconned thus this pacifist 6th generation Inconnu children of Marconius is on good relations with the local Garou and Fae communities to he point there is a pack of werewolves called the Sunstringers who protect Bartholomew\u2019s haven and consider him one of the few Kindred deserving of an existence and Bartholomew have a team of Goblins who will aid him as much as they can...<br /> <b>The Arcadian</b>'s name speak for itself I think<br /> <b>B\u00e9atrice L'Angou</b> from Montreal by Night on the other hand is a scholar, collector of knowledge, but <i>not</i> an innovator and the Path of Nocturnal Redemption (a Path of Enlightenment created by the members of the coven known as the Shepherds of Caine) she follows is a potent mixture of human faith and Cainite enlightenment BUT builds on the Cainite'S faith as a mortal, there is nothing new in it basically or revolutionary. Just a modified version something that already existed and was important to someone.<br /> <br /> Wouldn't say the Kiasyd are a 'good' representatives of the Vampire race and limitations, considering they are with one foot is in another setting<br /> Kiasyd Alchemy is a strange mixology with very weird effects and backgrounds\u200b\u200b<br /> All and all, okay, I give you that, the Kiasyd could (and should) be an exeption but you must admit, they are the wierdest breed you could find in the setting (or settings)\u200b<br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-25T16:10:07-07:00","id":1524508,"title":"","content":"One of the other things I have an issue with is that sometimes people think that elders and ancients would be tech phobic in general. I think they would keep an eye on technologies and trends that would help them hide better or take down their rivals more quickly.<br /> <br /> Karsh the Warlord Of The Camarilla would certainly keep an eye on military and intelligence gathering tech that would aid him or others in his position, and Vykos would certainly keep an eye on the latest medical and scientific advances that would aid it in many goals. You can bet the Nosferatu and Ventrue would use the social media to keep tabs on trends or events that might concern them.<br /> <br /> Some Kindred do have a spark of creativity left, but usually they take advantage of someone else's work and improve on it and take it in directions that others wouldn't consider at all. I personally go with the notion that being undead hasn't totally smothered the spark of creativity, but it's very hard for them to get out of old mindsets.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 10-25-2023, 07:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-25T16:54:20-07:00","id":1524514,"title":"","content":"I don't know if this is the case, but there was a VTM game where one of the characters was very good at hacking and this caused a lot of problems, because with creativity he basically solved any challenge that didn't require direct confrontation and everything is fun and until you need a password on an elder's multinational company computer and the guy manages to steal it with a laptop next to a trash can, yes that was an exaggeration, but not so much. In fact, drones can be scammed and are not necessarily discreet, so I think it's a good to use them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-26T02:03:32-07:00","id":1524517,"title":"","content":"I can\u2019t remember where it was, but there was a bit about Knowledge Ratings not necessarily being equal through time. 5 dots in Science in a Dark Ages game is a very different thing to 5 dots in Science in a Modern game. <br /> <br /> Sure, Tech and Computers at 5 dots makes you a \u201cvisionary\u201d, but you\u2019re still using current-era materials, manufacturing, and general technology. At best, I could see a character with those stats building a current-era robot. Building something from Cyberpunk 2077 would require dozens of technological leaps in advancement beyond what is possible today. <br /> <br /> Lastly, if you\u2019re wanting to build something like that, you\u2019d better also have Resources 5/Domain or Haven 5/Retainers 5, at a minimum, to represent the fact that these sorts of things can\u2019t exactly be built in a garage. The material cost of top-end robots is enormous, not to mention the equipment required to manufacture and assemble them. It\u2019s not just a case of \u201cI\u2019m super smart, let me roll to make my robot army\u201d.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27967-caerolion","name":"Caerolion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-26T04:52:14-07:00","id":1524520,"title":"","content":"As a side-great concept for a mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-26T15:06:51-07:00","id":1524551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1524318-why-is-vtm-so-allergic-to-a-character-being-an-inventor-visonary?p=1524505#post1524505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do they really creating?<br /> Or re-create, copy something they had as humans either Mages or shamans, priests, etc...?<br /> Every Thaumaturgical, Koldunic, Necromantic, Voudoun etc Path and Ritual had a Human equivalent down the line...<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Again, those philosophies and relegions are/were modified versions of pre-existing beief systems and relegions if we look them closely<br /> As much as the vampires love to bang their chest how &quot;inhumane&quot; those Paths are, most IF not all ofthem are actually quite... understandable from human point of view and you can find a human cult or sect or even a whole relegion that mirrored it or was very similar<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is that the same reasoning can be applied to humans. <br /> <br /> Most if not all innovations are iterations of/inspired by previous creations. Philosophies are built on previous ideas, religion synchretise ancient dogma, etc<br /> <br /> Same for magic in the setting. Yes, blood sorcery ressemble human magic, but whose to say which one inspired the other, or that two similar rituals aren't simply convergent creations? <br /> <br /> Same for kindred/human mutual influences. Did ancient nosferatus used the gauls' beliefs in cthonic deities to act as gods, or are they the source of those beliefs?<br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200bEven mages doesn't, if you pardon me the pun, conjures paradigms from the ether. They are inspired by previous ideas and the universe around them. <br /> <br /> \u00c0 tremere building a path of thaumaturgy based on ancient Greeks notion of divination by Dreams with a twist of tremere symbolism is hardly different from an engineer building a new machine based on the accumulated body of physics knowledge. <br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-27T05:37:22-07:00","id":1524584,"title":"","content":"[Forum ate it]<br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","user":"Shadeprowler","date":". 10-28-2023, 11:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-27T05:40:02-07:00","id":1524585,"title":"","content":"God I HATE THIS FLAGGING SYSTEM...<br /> Okay...<br /> Lets see<br /> <br /> <br /> Sure, but the whole argument could be &quot;solved&quot; by the Curse of Caine:<br /> Nothing can destroy Caine (this and the sevenfold extension comes from God - or an intermediate)<br /> Then the Angels added the &quot;traditional&quot; vampiric cuses with a lovely addition:<br /> Everything he creates (his children, they\u2019re children and so on) are doomed as well and and suffer as well to increase his suffering by watching his failure unfold. - this one he managed to pass on to his descendants<br /> This (and the fact Humanity is HUGE - the population of Earth is <i>8,068,973,367</i> as of Friday, October 27, 2023 - and among of those 8 billion souls how many are... inventors? When it comes to numbers, inventors and visionaries are patheticly low) basically guarantees, even if you were one of the very - I mean VERY - few geniuses, visionary inventors as a Human, after the Embrace even if it not gone, but just fades... you are doomed by faliure and to watch the effect of that faliure. You are cursed<br /> As a Vampire your inability to really create and innovate - or do manage to create and watch it crumble and fail - is part of the personan horror thing.<br /> The nature of Cain's Curse is to wander until the end of all things always with regret in his heart. Regret that he killed his beloved brother for nothing, regret that he did as God asked and was punished instead, regret that the only way to save himself or humanity is to admit he was wrong and beg for God's forgiveness.<br /> (If you want to toss some crossover, we could drag the Weaver and Stasis connection to this, but not really needed)<br /> Of course, ultimately it is up to the storyteller how interpret things and treat them as part of their chronicle<br /> Gehenna hinted for example, Caine cursed himself in that Garden, not God. It was that realization that led to the weakening of vampires, as the curses faded. So Caine was an awakened mage, and the architect of his own suffering, which continued so long as he deemed it to be. As he Curse fade, you don't even need Gehenna, just Caine to come terms of himself - things could change<br /> Or some vampire cults don't see vampirism as a curse but as a gift. Abel's sacrifice for a lamb pleased God more than Cains sacrifice of grain but it was Cains sacrifice of his own brothers blood that pleased God the most. To these Kindred vampires are avenging angels ordained by God to free the souls of mortals trapped in material bodies, so no limitations<br /> According to the Cainite Heresy, Cain is not just cursed, but God made him and Angel and his powers are the powers of being the Angel of Murder. This line of thought was created in the dark ages and had a comeback recently...<br /> Anyhow, at the end of the day, it is up to the storyteller, but there are very good argument why vampires are unable to <i>really</i> create and innovate, to be visionaries\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-27T14:31:29-07:00","id":1524606,"title":"","content":"I remember in some of the Gehenna options that members of the Gangrel &amp; Nosferatu clan found themselves looking more and more human looking Shadowprowler .","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-27T19:58:52-07:00","id":1524612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1524318-why-is-vtm-so-allergic-to-a-character-being-an-inventor-visonary#post1524318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe someone in the past mentioned here that inventor/visonary character builds don't see much use due to the ST's not wanting any change to the setting, and after playing for a while, that feeling seems to be somewhat common. My question is, why? As long as you are not going too crazy and making nuclear weapons or spaceships in the early 1900's, I don't see why it would be that large of an issue. I have also noticed that at times ST's will refrence real life science when talking about how it is unlikely for characters to make certain innovations.<br /> <br /> Which doesn't really make much sense to me. There are characters which are breaking the laws of nature using magic and disciplines, comparatively, what some of my characters were doing was much more tame. Plus, if someone has 5 in tech and computers, why can't they make robots somewhat similar to those found in cyberpunk 2077? From what I remember, having 5 in an ability makes you a vissonary in that field, and in STEM, there's always some advancement.</div> </div> </div> </div>In Truth, a &quot;Tony Stark&quot; or even a Bruce Wayne or Macguyver guys are completely unrealistic. RPGs are fantastic in nature thou... When you buy &quot;Science Skill 5&quot; would basically be some insane intellect that would make Einstein look illiterate.<br /> <br /> In real life, you have people who are experts in their fields... And pretty much nothing else. Someone brilliant (say, like Einstein) can revolutionize their field... But not improve the Science and Technology of the world for the next era. Einstein revolutionized Physics, but our GPS machines would only come almost a century later.<br /> <br /> Those &quot;Visionary&quot; technological leaps are the result of THOUSANDS (or more) of competent (and many brilliant amongst those) people building up on the work of those before them.<br /> <br /> Like Newton said &quot;if I managed to look ahead, it's because I stood in the shoulders of giants&quot;.<br /> <br /> Instead of a single unrealistic and cinematographic &quot;Super Genius&quot; building automatons using just Steampunk engineering, you actually need incremental steps done by thousands of scientists, engineers and mathematicians each contributing over dozens of different fields and hundreds of different specializations.<br /> <br /> A better computer requires hundreds (or thousands) of microprocessor engineers, hundreds (or thousands) of programmers, and several other fields, and no single person is capable of doing it all by themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-27T20:23:40-07:00","id":1524613,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1524318-why-is-vtm-so-allergic-to-a-character-being-an-inventor-visonary?p=1524362#post1524362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is a True Brujah merit, called <b>Advanced Tech</b> (1-5 pt. Merit) [Lore of Bloodline p. 99]<br /> You have a device (or possibly a few) of an advanced design. While the True Brujah are not especially good at innovation, they are good at making improvements. So this device has no special functions unavailable to its contemporaries, but it does work a lot better. It reduces the chance of a mechanical fault (such as a jam) by half and all uses of the device are made with a -1 to the difficulty. The Storyteller should decide on the cost of the Merit, depending on how many items the character has, and how powerful they are.<br /> <br /> To reflect what the narrator True Brujah says about technology and science:<br /> <br /> &quot;<i>We are not just collectors of lore, but also students of it. With the vast resources at our command, we stand on the shoulders of giants when it comes to scientific advancement. While it is too dangerous to share the fruits of our labor with other Kindred or the kine, we do release some advancements into kine society when we need humanity to catch up.<br /> Now you would think that any scientist, given eternity and the best resources, would be able to change the world, cure cancer, develop true artificial intelligence, and more. Unfortunately, it has proved not to be the case. While our scientists are both dedicated and extremely intelligent, they are not innovators.<br /> It seems that the spark of creation and inspiration turns to ash when we become Kindred. It is a problem that haunts many of our most academic elders.<br /> That is not to say we waste our time, though.<br /> While we rarely innovate, we are very, very good at making improvements.<br /> Our technology does little that is new, but works much better and faster than its modern counterpart. This can often be an advantage, as it makes it easy to hide among less advanced equipment. For instance, our computers are simply faster than those available to humanity, even if they are not intelligent or organic</i>.&quot;\u200b<br /> <br /> It is nicely summarize this whole discussion<br /> Even with <i>literally all the time of the world </i>a vampire only manage to impove, but not <i>really</i> innovate</div> </div> </div> </div>That's exactly what I would say. Instead of creating teleporting machines, self replicating intelligent robots or trans-dimensional projectors, your visionary vampire could make things better. Imagine a vampire hacker with Computer 5 that also has a super computer with the juiciest of the bonuses possible. Imagine that your hand guns or fully automatic rifles give several bonuses; your security system is better than Fort Knox and so forth so on.<br /> <br /> Sure, Hit Marks are impressive beasts, but just &quot;simply&quot; having what everybody else has but simply better, already is a massive advantage. Computers for instance are powerful tools, so imagine having not just the best possible model, but one slightly better than that. Get a bullet proof car with machine guns, fire throwers and a maneuverability unequal to even the best Lamborghinis around, ABS breaks that are better than anything around - basically a car that would keep alive and ALMOST eliminate the possibility of accidents for even someone suffering a drug induced psychosis episode. Or a sword made with heavy material (for example, depleted Uranium) and Kevlar, making it the ideal tool for someone with Potence and Celerity (possibly with an edge that has been sharpened with laser, turning it into a &quot;monowire&quot;, the cutting edge is reduced to the size of atoms, or perhaps it also is a &quot;vibroblade&quot;).<br /> <br /> That's the kind of improvements that would be within the scope of the game and proper for a &quot;super genius&quot; type of character<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-28T15:22:25-07:00","id":1524661,"title":"","content":"Just to be clear, I was referring to things like drones. Not anything crazy like teleportation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-28T15:26:18-07:00","id":1524664,"title":"","content":"Thinking on this discussion, it might be doable as thaumaturgy/blood sorcery is conventionally hermetic magic then logically a technocratic paradime would left you 'invent' high tech stuff. This would effectively let you brucr wayne/Tony stark it without breaking the in setting logic.<br /> <br /> As a side the idea of house tremere using technocracy rather than hermetic is an fascinating and disturbing idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-28T16:03:03-07:00","id":1524665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Joanna_Crone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1524318-why-is-vtm-so-allergic-to-a-character-being-an-inventor-visonary?p=1524323#post1524323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, early VtM 1 was somewhat about these things. Vampire Louis Pasteur was killed via political machinations specifically because he was an innovator as you describe - he canonically made a serum first to turn humans to vamps, then one to turn vamps into humans. Before the game began to solidify itself as Blood Weeping Simulator, it was quite willing to explore a multitude of themes. Early WoD was absolutely willing to get gonzo, and it's in that environment that your character might thrive.</div> </div> </div> </div>When I first read about him, I was extremely surprised by how he was just killed off and how everything regarding the seum was brushed under the rug. It would have worked well with the current theme of the game in which the pc is supposed to be suffering from the curse of being an undying immortal and struggling to keep their humanity intact.<br /> <br /> The instructions on how to make it would be sought after by many vampires for a multitude of reasons. I really feel that it could have added a lot to the metaplot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-29T07:04:06-07:00","id":1524689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1524318-why-is-vtm-so-allergic-to-a-character-being-an-inventor-visonary?p=1524664#post1524664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thinking on this discussion, it might be doable as thaumaturgy/blood sorcery is conventionally hermetic magic then logically a technocratic paradime would left you 'invent' high tech stuff. This would effectively let you brucr wayne/Tony stark it without breaking the in setting logic.<br /> <br /> As a side the idea of house tremere using technocracy rather than hermetic is an fascinating and disturbing idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, House Tremere was an ardent defender of the Masquerade after their &quot;embrace&quot; (be it an act of Magick or an embrace comme il faut) and all in all one of the forces behind the Camarilla. Their treason was one of the reasons that put the Order of Reason on the map and fundamentally changed the paradigm.<br /> <br /> And about the Toreador lacking creativity, that may be seen as an attempt to force the angsty themes than a reality. Beckett after all said that there were vampires both stubborn to change and pretty creative. I guess there is no rule set in stone that say that all vampires are incapable to create and change, given the Masquerade and the jihad. Down the line, is mostly up to the character and GM.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27825-mrdrika","name":"MrDrika","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27825_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-29T07:06:26-07:00","id":1524690,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1524318-why-is-vtm-so-allergic-to-a-character-being-an-inventor-visonary?p=1524501#post1524501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The extra diegetic reason for it is evident, the writers don't want the rational vampires to have futurist tech.<br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>It's no coincidence the bloodline with the time manipulation and perception discipline, is the one to have a unique merit related to possessing near-future tech. Much the same as the one with the body modification discipline, is the one to have unique merits related to body modification of any and all sorts. Just food for thought.<br /> <br /> It's also the case VtM, contrary to how it's presented in the metaplot, is best played as a street-level game which means things can't necessarily get <i>too</i> gonzo. If we're going with comparisons to MtAs, your Trujah is more likely to have an X-5 Protector, armor cloth business suit, or black sedan (minus the Mind and Forces stuff) than they are a plasma cannon, exosuit, or VDAS implant. Believe me when I say the three examples I mentioned as something a Trujah might have, is more than adequate. That really strikes to the bigger problem -- players tend strongly towards the wild, outlandish, impractical, and borderline-if-not-outright un-judiciable stuff when it comes to things like this.<br /> <br /> As said up-thread, they want to be Tony Stark building ridiculous and wildly impractical crap like power armor, opposed to running a chop shop which would let the PC launder, customize, up-armor, or disappear vehicles in the city. They want to be Mark Zuckerberg, not the vampire who surreptitiously dropped a kinky hook-up app on the mobile stores which lets vampires find preferred victims without needing a herd or endangering the Masquerade. They want to be Jeff Bezos, not the vampire who runs a server farm in a basement somewhere that parses local news feeds, community forums and law enforcement scanners, and algorithmically processes that to identify and track hunters, and predict their activities -- or runs a bot farm fouling up the signal-to-noise ratio on the same online spaces, to disrupt and foil hunters. They want to be Elon Musk, not a vampire who holds a few key patents, and launders royalties for Resources 3 or 4.<br /> <br /> Those are the kinds of things players should be targeting when building for high Computers, Science, or Technology ratings, not comic book-y pulp stuff. They're all lower-key, more easily integrated into a chronicle, easier to adjudicate, more practical, and more importantly <i>deliver higher returns for PC's in the chronicle as it plays out than any more-gonzo alternative</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-29T12:21:03-07:00","id":1524699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrDrika</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1524318-why-is-vtm-so-allergic-to-a-character-being-an-inventor-visonary?p=1524689#post1524689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, House Tremere was an ardent defender of the Masquerade after their &quot;embrace&quot; (be it an act of Magick or an embrace comme il faut) and all in all one of the forces behind the Camarilla. Their treason was one of the reasons that put the Order of Reason on the map and fundamentally changed the paradigm.<br /> <br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>yeah, it'd require a seperate canon or an extraordinary series of events to be fully realised. But it's an interesting concept, In praxis you'd use paths and rituals to construct sinister vampire style tech.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-29T12:45:30-07:00","id":1524703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrDrika</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1524318-why-is-vtm-so-allergic-to-a-character-being-an-inventor-visonary?p=1524689#post1524689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, House Tremere was an ardent defender of the Masquerade after their &quot;embrace&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Those totally Masquarade-friendly Gargoyles are a prime example of that<br /> True, the 1489 Montmartre Pact forced them to vowe to never again create Gargoyles, releasing all under their control and ceasing to hunt those that had fled their rule. In exchange, the Gangrel and Nosferatu would abide any hostilities and the Tremere would be allowed to join the Camarilla...<br /> But still, the Tremere showed they are not really above to create artifical monstorsities<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1524318-why-is-vtm-so-allergic-to-a-character-being-an-inventor-visonary?p=1524699#post1524699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> yeah, it'd require a seperate canon or an extraordinary series of events to be fully realised. But it's an interesting concept, In praxis you'd use paths and rituals to construct sinister vampire style tech.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed<br /> But as they created the Gargoyles out of Nosferatu, Gangrel and Tzimisce &quot;prisoners of War&quot; to defend themselves, it is easy to make from point A to point B especially with the existence of Path of Technomancy, Path of Transmutation and Biothaumaturgy\u200b to make horrors that would make Phyrexia proud...<br /> After all, Victorian Age vampire Companion had Dr. Thomas Fountaindike, a 11th generation Giovanni who developed a method of binding the soul of a vampire called Marcello to an automaton resulting in what he called the Motorised Man. He dubbed the proceeding &quot;soulcrafting&quot;, and was consumed by the idea to create another intelligent automaton...<br /> So the building blocks of a more... Technocratic Tremere Clan is there for a GM to make the World of Darkness a bit more darker and sinister (and if you want to make things more bleak, just throw the Shinzui Industries and even Mikaboshi\u200b's &quot;emissaries&quot; from his Wicked City bearing gifts of technology from Hell...)\u200b<br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","user":"Shadeprowler","date":". 10-29-2023, 03:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-29T12:57:01-07:00","id":1524704,"title":"","content":"Damn it, one would think ~10 min woould be enough not to be flaged on editing<br /> Well, guess what<br /> Whataver...<br /> So<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrDrika</strong> <a 