nt A to point B especially with the existence of Path of Technomancy, Path of Transmutation and Biothaumaturgy\u200b to make horrors that would make Phyrexia proud...<br /> After all, Victorian Age vampire Companion had Dr. Thomas Fountaindike, a 11th generation Giovanni who developed a method of binding the soul of a vampire called Marcello to an automaton resulting in what he called the Motorised Man. He dubbed the proceeding &quot;soulcrafting&quot;, and was consumed by the idea to create another intelligent automaton...<br /> So the building blocks of a more... Technocratic Tremere Clan is there for a GM to make the World of Darkness a bit more darker and sinister (and if you want to make things more bleak, just throw the Shinzui Industries and even Mikaboshi\u200b's &quot;emissaries&quot; from his Wicked City bearing His gifts of technology from Hell...)\u200b<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","user":"Shadeprowler","date":". 10-30-2023, 03:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-29T16:47:00-07:00","id":1524718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1524318-why-is-vtm-so-allergic-to-a-character-being-an-inventor-visonary?p=1524704#post1524704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Indeed<br /> But as they created the Gargoyles out of Nosferatu, Gangrel and Tzimisce &quot;prisoners of War&quot; to defend themselves, it is easy to make from point A to point B especially with the existence of Path of Technomancy, Path of Transmutation and Biothaumaturgy\u200b to make horrors that would make Phyrexia proud...<br /> After all, Victorian Age vampire Companion had Dr. Thomas Fountaindike, a 11th generation Giovanni who developed a method of binding the soul of a vampire called Marcello to an automaton resulting in what he called the Motorised Man. He dubbed the proceeding &quot;soulcrafting&quot;, and was consumed by the idea to create another intelligent automaton...<br /> So the building blocks of a more... Technocratic Tremere Clan is there for a GM to make the World of Darkness a bit more darker and sinister (and if you want to make things more bleak, just throw the Shinzui Industries and even Mikaboshi\u200b's &quot;emissaries&quot; from his Wicked City bearing Hia gifts of technology from Hell...)\u200b<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>yeah some of stuff i came up with.<br /> <br /> -predatorial mosquito like drones.<br /> <br /> -Some sort of human blood milking machine<br /> <br /> -a killer robot fuelled by blood.<br /> <br /> -ghouled anthrax<br /> <br /> -high tech weaponry enhanced by vitae. Eg rail guns<br /> <br /> -online programmes which transfer Dominate commands.<br /> <br /> -blank clones for Dominate 5.<br /> <br /> The horrible sky's the limit.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-30T00:07:23-07:00","id":1524738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1524318-why-is-vtm-so-allergic-to-a-character-being-an-inventor-visonary?p=1524718#post1524718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> yeah some of stuff i came up with.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Love the way you think ^^\u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1524318-why-is-vtm-so-allergic-to-a-character-being-an-inventor-visonary?p=1524718#post1524718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> -ghouled anthrax<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Funny you mentioned that<br /> <br /> Tzimsice clanbook Revised took that rute - kind of:<br /> &quot;So, to better protect our interests, a number of our brightest members infiltrated the Soviet Union\u2019s Ministry of Medical and Microbiological Industries, a quiet euphemism for their bioweapons program under the Main Intelligence Directorate (GRU).Called Biopreparat, the Russians worked to develop new strains and vectors for diseases ranging from typhus to Ebola.<br /> Some young Fiends even played at developing Cainite pathogens that targeted specific clans, blood viruses that could turn entire populations into our ghouls or even methods of turning viruses into microbial ghouls.\u200b<br /> We insured that nearly three generations of Obertus revenants learned a dizzying array of the new sciences including biochemistry, epidemiology, virology and microbiology.<br /> Soon, our spies found work in hidden facilities at \u201cRebirth Island\u201d in the Aral Sea and at Solovetsky, the nexus prison camp of the gulags.<br /> Unfortunately, while our ghouls made some advancements, particularly in the field of recombinant DNA and socalled chimerical viruses, the Soviet Union collapsed.&quot;<br /> <br /> Staying on topic, it is important to mention, the Tzimsice used Ravenants to make the scientific studies for them - sure, probably more than one of those learned Obertus (Oberti?) were Embraced but as the Clanbook said: &quot;Several key ghouls also vanished with their research, sending us scrambling to find them. To date, we\u2019ve had little success...&quot;<br /> A little ooops, but still, the important is, even the ghouls had limited success (so one could argue, the Ravenants, who are &quot;tainted&quot; by their blood are not immune the Vampires's curse of faliure&quot;) and they were smart Humans (or at least as close to a Human as you can get without being a Vampire)<br /> <br /> Then again, similarly in the Clanbook it is mentioned:\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> <br /> &quot;Anyway, getting back to Piotr; his specialists think that the Ebola they\u2019ve found in various outbreaks is a poisonous by-product of something larger.<br /> Piotr called it ghoul bacteria, but he couldn\u2019t be sure.<br /> What they found in Kitum Cave, however, is fluid and won\u2019t stay locked down. They\u2019re not sure what it is exactly, but they have a fair idea.<br /> Here\u2019s what our Russian friends think, and remember, I\u2019m just the messenger.<br /> They think Demdemeh transcended all right, but not in the way we\u2019d expect. Piotr believes he obliterated himself into viral form, then used his own childer as petri dishes.<br /> They found that protean viral sample in Kitum on a dying elephant. Piotr thinks the Methuselah is infecting the local wildlife (\u201criding elephants\u201d he called it) and occasionally vectoring Ebola into the populace.&quot;<br /> <br /> So again, Canon actually helps a Storyteller here - examples exist in the setting, the rest is just clever usage of it<br /> Maybe in that setting the Tremere - who were created by Tzimsice blood - managed to isolate the Vicissitude &quot;strain&quot; and refine it... weaponize it...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1524318-why-is-vtm-so-allergic-to-a-character-being-an-inventor-visonary?p=1524718#post1524718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> -blank clones for Dominate 5.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> <br /> Lobotomy was a regular practice used by the tzimisce in the creation of ghouls that could more easily be puppeted with dominate<br /> Sooo...<br /> Anyway, the Settite Sorcery, Akhu got that covered (sort of)<br /> I mean the &quot;cloning&quot; part to a sense<br /> The Path of Ushabti<br /> When creating those servants, with 5 success, the creation is: &quot;Indistinguishable from a living creature&quot; and the 5th level,Gift of Khnum allows the sorcerer to create what is effectively a living body, either as an obedient slave or as a ready-made vessel for a wraith or a spirit.<br /> Again, the basics are there<br /> Not really cloning, by machines or magic, true... but a good start<br /> <br /> Just for funsies, we already did it... in a sense; in 2019:<br /> The twins, called Lulu and Nana, reportedly had their genes modified before birth by a Chinese scientific team using the new editing tool CRISPR. The goal was to make the girls immune to infection by HIV, the virus that causes AIDS. Now, new research shows that the same alteration introduced into the girls\u2019 DNA, deletion of a gene called CCR5, not only makes mice smarter but also improves human brain recovery after stroke, and could be linked to greater success in school.<br /> This is more like eugenics, true, but since cloning (with cows, pigs, sheeps, etc) are &quot;working&quot; - the one thing that keeps us cloning humans are morality issues, not scientific limtiations<br /> And the same method that made allegedly those girls smarter... could work in the other way or be totally blank, with the proper limitations <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-30T03:31:48-07:00","id":1524742,"title":"","content":"Yeah it makes sense the fiends would be up for to that sort of thing. They're probably the most magey clan next to the tremere. I think a lot of groundwork for technocracy thaumaturges in other effects. A lot of time you'd be talking about how it's done. For example path of levingbolt with an energy weapon instead of murming some latin/enochian and genrally more sci fi themed rituals.<br /> <br /> a friend of mine actually did a series of write ups of what it'd be like if tremere had belonged to a differant da tradition/craft and how it would have played out. The Al I baitini and chorus imploded and the Valderman resulted in a major series of divergence in the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 10-30-2023, 06:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-30T05:43:19-07:00","id":1524753,"title":"","content":"If you have Int 5(+) and Science 5(+) you may possess Theoretical Knowledge beyond the bounds of modern Technology to test let alone implement, near on 40 years ago I knew a University Professor in his 50's multiple PHD's, got a friend who kept in touch with him he has told me by the time Math had advanced enough for other scientests to test his proofs (about ten years ago) the professor had long retired and today Technology has just reached a level to perhaps build experimental equipment to start to advance his work, but last I'd heard of the Professor was invalid and in fast deteriorating health and given the timetable I was told he was on he should be dead by now.<br /> <br /> Lifespan may not be a factor for a kindred, but Int 5(+) and Science 5(+) means there may be only a handful of people on the planet who can understand you work and you nor they could likely make the rest of the scientific community truly understand it let alone put it to particle use or make even normal very smart people understand it enough to understand it's significance let alont the work itself. you would be like Babbage and his Difference Engine only without the benefit of Ada Lovelace.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28255-dropbear","name":"DropBear","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-04T15:30:05-07:00","id":1525037,"title":"","content":"Visionaries are already rare in humans.<br /> <br /> Some of them are public figures, making embracing them a masquerade breach.<br /> <br /> Vampires mostly embrace because of pasion or because they need a powerful servant/a soldier. A visionary could prove difficult to control or even surpass the sire. Yes, methusaleah may embrace a visionary but that is because they trust the age gap for control.<br /> <br /> Even the most passionate vampires have to deal with the night to nigh politics to the point that they do not have as much time to innovate. The place where you live and the amount of lights hours also influences your activity a lot.<br /> <br /> However there are visionaries, thaumaturgy is a blood work in constant development, I remember a ritual that allowed to use blood magick as an app or something similar. The tremere built their core discipline from zero because they lost their awakened magick etc... There are those who make their combo disciplines and you can import the Ordo Dracul if you want the scientist vampire in your games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24037-leandro16","name":"Leandro16","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24037_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-05T10:32:05-08:00","id":1525077,"title":"","content":"I seem to remember in the revised Ventrue clan book that they shy away from embracing such public figures as they didn\u2019t do well being at the bottom of kindred society. I would have a hard time picturing Alexander The Great being disrespected by people he would consider barbaric or folks like Julius or Augustus Ceasor who are used to being top dog.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-06T20:39:54-08:00","id":1525147,"title":"","content":"Well, if we are talking about &quot;techno-thaumaturgy&quot; then things are entirely different.<br /> <br /> I thought we were only speaking about &quot;mundane&quot; Technology. If we give it a magical spin, things are totally different.<br /> <br /> A robot animated by vitae ain't much different from a Golem.<br /> <br /> If we add magic, then the &quot;techno&quot; part becomes more aesthetic than anything.<br /> <br /> If we are talking about REAL &quot;mundane&quot; technologies (if we can call those magic mirrors we all carry in our pockets and that has the entire collection of human knowledge as &quot;mundane&quot;), then things are a lot less fantastic, but we can still take a few &quot;cinematographic&quot; liberties.<br /> <br /> Drones, computers and smartphones are impressive things by themselves, double so when they are the top of the line military grade. If you &quot;just&quot; take what already is the best that is and make it just slightly better, then we are talking about some real powerful toys over here.<br /> <br /> Take ChatGPT for instance, as impressive as it is; currently this is version 4.0.<br /> <br /> Now, if you tell me that the &quot;techno-leeches&quot; are always at least 1 or even 2 versions ahead of the curve, a group of blood suckers playing with ChatGPT 5 or maybe 6+, is VERY impressive. That alone could be quasi Technocracy levels of capability.<br /> <br /> Now for drones, have you guys watched the movie Sonic? Those Dr Robotinik's drones, that's not something too out of the realm of possibilities. Or the drones that Tony Stark gave to Peter Parker and that got used by Mysterio in the movie of Spider Man. Drones with military grade machine guns, perhaps with explosive ammunition, grenade launchers or flamethrowers, kamikase drones with napalm and so on.<br /> <br /> For weapons and vehicles, here too there's room for improvement. Explosive ammunitions, incendiary ammunitions (white phosphorus maybe?). Vibroblade swords with a monowire cut (vibroblade swords have a battery that is used for the blade to slightly vibrate, causing the impacts to be much more devastating, while a monowire cut is obtained by sharpening the blade with a laser, making it to be so thin to the point of being sharpened at an atomic level, causing cuts almost at a molecular level).<br /> <br /> With material sciences, your ultra tech blade could be made of high dense materials - say, depleted Uranium for instance - and highly resistant (imagine combining depleted Uranium and Kevlar or some such). This would be ideal for those Potence users, but even regular humans could pack a much harder punch with an extra heavy blade<br /> <br /> On top of it, it could have a highly sophisticated system (controlled by AI maybe?) with small thrusters that increase the movement momentum, adding to the impact.<br /> <br /> Combine all of the above for some &quot;super tech sword&quot; without a single drop of ocus pocus magic.<br /> <br /> I recommend the book &quot;Gurps Ultra Tech&quot; for ideas on the &quot;mundane&quot; technologies of the tomorrow. This book is simply put the BEST possible for any one trying to introduce that little bit of cyberpunk into their games. It discusses everything you could possibly imagine - from medicine to energy (sources and storage), machines, vehicles, computers, computer programs and more.<br /> <br /> Just as a quick explanation: GURPS divide the technologies in &quot;Technological Levels&quot;. So, &quot;TL&quot; 0 is the Stone Age, TL 1 Bronze Age, TL 2 Iron Age, TL 3 Middle Ages, TL 4 is the Age of Sails. Those are described on &quot;Gurps Low Tech&quot;, another incredible book, and if you guys are playing any DA game, I 101% recommend; seriously, there's stuff there that I could never even have imagined<br /> <br /> Things start to get interesting at TL 5 - Steam Age. Early Industrial Revolution.<br /> TL 6 is the age of oil<br /> TL 7 is the atomic age<br /> And finally, TL 8\u200b is the Age of Information, the Age we are in.<br /> <br /> TL 5 to TL 8 are covered on GURPS High Tech, so if you want to play some Victorian Era, WW2 or Modern day, this is the book. Again, incredible source, and it enriched any game. Also, if you seek to just tweak a bit with what we already have, that's your toolbox<br /> <br /> But, if you want the truly crazy stuff, you'll want GURPS Ultra Tech. This one sounds like a &quot;Guide to the Technocracy&quot; but without all of the more &quot;exoteric&quot; parts.<br /> <br /> Here, Gurps creates 4 additional theoretical TLs, from 9 to TL 12.<br /> TL 9 - Microtech Age<br /> TL 10 - Robotic Age<br /> TL 11 - Age of Exotic Matter<br /> TL 12 - Age of Miracles <br /> <br /> So, anything at TL 9 is acceptable. In fact, since the publishing of the book, many of the, at the time, theoretical technologies disposed at the TL 9 are either very close to being created NOW or are being prototyped already. Really, it is impressive.<br /> <br /> Things at TL 10 sometimes are alright, sometimes are outlandish, so do consider them carefully.<br /> <br /> Things at TL 11 are completely bonks, unless you truly want some silly &quot;Techno-Vamp Star Trek&quot; I wouldn't use those.<br /> <br /> And TL 12 is basically the &quot;Precursor Race&quot; who is so Technologically advanced that can shape reality with their thoughts (or so it seems). TL 12 is basically the stage upon which technology becomes indistinguishable from magic, so don't bother with this <br /> <br /> The book also makes a distinction between what is not just possible technologies but also PROBABLE ones, and some others that are deemed as &quot;Super Science&quot;. So, just so you know, &quot;Super Science&quot; is any outlandish thing that contradicts what we CURRENTLY know about the Sciences. Therefore, any sort of communication and/or transportation that is FTL (faster than light) is automatically deemed as &quot;Super Science&quot;. So, it is up to the GM to allow any of those or not, since those may well be in the field of fantasy.<br /> <br /> On the other hand thou, the theory of Relativity would be considered as &quot;Super Science&quot; (aka Fantasy) for a 19th century scientist, so you may allow those based on that premisse that, perhaps, we just don't think those things are possible because we lack the knowledge of how they are possible to begin with.<br /> <br /> Take a look into those 3 books, it is amazing.<br /> <br /> And, if you guys love your little pet Franksteins, get also GURPS Bio Tech. Complete with everything from Artificial Selection (starting at TL 0 from the Stone Age) all the way up to &quot;Bio-Buildings&quot; and &quot;Bio-Starships&quot; at the TL 12 Age of Miracles, with everything in-between (cloning, DNA manipulation and many more).<br /> <br /> By the way, the many advantages and Disadvantages in those books, particularly on Bio Tech, are super easy to adapt for WoD (heck, I would say that the ones on WoD were adapted from Gurps to begin with). Many of those in Bio Tech could be used even for vampires.<br /> \u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-06T21:04:31-08:00","id":1525148,"title":"","content":"I'll give you guys 2 examples from Gurps Bio Tech (4ed):<br /> <br /> &quot;INSECT BIOWEAPONS (TL9)<br /> Insect bioweapons are usually stored as vials of eggs and<br /> released into still water; in a few hours, days or weeks, they<br /> will hatch into tens of thousands of insects.<br /> An area might be seeded with biting insects, such as<br /> horseflies or blackflies. Multiple bites cause irritation (-1 on<br /> DX and IQ until treated) and prevent anyone from getting<br /> any sleep (resulting in fatigue). A sealed suit or the Sealed<br /> advantage protects against this.<br /> Other insect bioweapons might be given more subtle<br /> targets. While sending genemod moths with a programmed<br /> desire to eat the enemy\u2019s uniforms is probably more an<br /> exercise in whimsy than anything else, a plague of unsea-<br /> sonal pests that eat crops or get into stored grain is no<br /> laughing matter, especially if they\u2019ve been altered to resist<br /> the usual pesticides.<br /> For greater lethality, insect pests could be infected to<br /> carry genemod plagues dangerous to humans or other ani-<br /> mals. Often, bloodsucking, winged insects are chosen, such<br /> as mosquitoes (which can already carry several diseases).<br /> In game terms, anyone traveling through an area infested\u200b<br /> with plague-carrying insects is treated as being in a disease-<br /> ridden area (see Contagion, p. B443); roll at -2 if they lack<br /> appropriate repellent, insect-resistant clothing or force<br /> fields.<br /> Genetic modification can be used to make an insect<br /> bioweapon much more useful. The insects could be<br /> designed so that they will not attack if they detect certain<br /> chemical cues \u2013 which are often odors below the human<br /> olfactory threshold. That way, you can protect your own<br /> people with a specialized form of repellent.<br /> For even greater precision, insect<br /> weapons could be programmed to home in<br /> on a specific chemical cue and only attack<br /> targets that give it off. This is easy if the<br /> enemy are another species, but if (for<br /> instance) the enemy uses a particular food,<br /> lubricant, or laundry detergent and none of<br /> the local civilians or your own people do,<br /> then you can gengineer your insects to go<br /> after them and leave everyone else alone.<br /> For the enemy to discover what was hap-<br /> pening, they would have to first trace any<br /> plague to the insects, dissect an insect to understand what<br /> molecules it is reacting to, then correlate this with the<br /> odors of all their equipment and supplies. Even with chem-<br /> ical sensors and computer analysis, this could take weeks.<br /> A more trial-and-error approach would be to leave out cer-<br /> tain supplies to see if the insects are attracted to them in the<br /> absence of humans.<br /> Another modification that could make insect weapons<br /> nastier is to redesign them to be resistant to certain com-<br /> mon types of insect repellent, or to have pan-specific poi-<br /> son resistance. A pesticide that kills any insect can be engi-<br /> neered, but this may fatally damage the ecosystem (killing<br /> beneficial insects or plants) and have toxic short- or long-<br /> term effects on human health as well.<br /> The best ways to deal with genemod insects may be<br /> swarms of engineered defensive insects, target-seeking<br /> viruses, tiny microbots, or nano-machines.\u200b&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> [B]That however was just TL 9 (the very next age after our current one). Now, let's see some of the outlandish stuff of the far future:[\\b]<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Sponge Computers (TL10)<br /> Sponges have a homogeneous macroscopic structure<br /> suitable for hosting neural networks, but the natural ani-<br /> mals do not take advantage of this to perform complex<br /> thinking. With some genetic tinkering, sponges can be<br /> made to grow electrically active neurons in configurations<br /> responsive to external stimuli. As these develop, they<br /> become effectively \u201cartificial brains,\u201d that can be connected<br /> to biosensors or other electronics. Sponge computers<br /> incorporate memories and make logical connections much<br /> like a real brain, with the advantages that the structure<br /> allows the permeation of nutrients and oxygen and that<br /> they can keep growing as long as these are supplied. They<br /> are thus much more robust than vatbrains and easier to<br /> grow.<br /> At TL11, sponge computer implants can be made with<br /> discriminatory growth patterns that let them grow into<br /> small crevices and infiltrate biological material. Implanted<br /> into a sinus cavity, it could grow into and either supple-<br /> ment or take over the brain of a person. Use the rules for<br /> vatbrains (p. 28) but halve the cost and weight. There is no<br /> practical upper limit to how large a sponge computer can<br /> be \u2013 they can be housed in the open ocean if necessary.<br /> TL11 infiltrative sponge computer implants most often<br /> suppress higher brain functions, giving the subject both the<br /> AI and Automaton meta-traits (p. B263). They are about the<br /> size of an apple seed and can be easily implanted in food,<br /> etc. They take a day to grow; a HT-4 roll means the subject\u2019s<br /> immune system fended them off. Removal requires brain<br /> surgery, much like removing a tumor; roll at -3 if they\u2019re<br /> half-grown or -6 if full-grown.\u200b<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Fungal Infonets (TL10)<br /> Transgenic sequences can grow neural tissue within<br /> fungal threads, allowing them to act as conduits for elec-<br /> trochemical signals. This means fungi can build \u201cwires\u201d<br /> and \u201ccircuits\u201d on and within any medium in which they can<br /> grow \u2013 which is just about anywhere. By planting such a<br /> fungus, one can grow circuitry in places where building it<br /> by more intrusive means would be too difficult or too<br /> noticeable. Special nodes in the fungus allow connections<br /> to be made to conventional electrical circuitry, or other<br /> organisms that can send and interpret signals through the<br /> fungal net.<br /> <br /> Fungal Surveillance Net (TL11)<br /> With their ability to grow on anything and their tenden-<br /> cy to be ignored or overlooked by people, fungal infonets<br /> make ideal infiltration organisms. Further gengineered<br /> enhancements can add organs sensitive to light, sound, and<br /> chemical stimuli, turning them into organic surveillance<br /> systems that can be installed simply by spreading spores.<br /> \u200b<br /> Smart Fungi (TL11)<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200bBy concentrating neural tissue into distributed process- ing nodes, a fungal infonet can be modified to allow a more<br /> coordinated reaction of the entire organism to local stim-<br /> uli. Although a far cry from true intelligence, this gives the<br /> fungus rudimentary problem-solving capability and allows<br /> it to seek particular targets to grow into and digest. When<br /> combined with acidic or parasitic properties, this produces<br /> an insidious biological weapon.<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> Intelligent Fungi (TL12)<br /> Further enhancements give fungi neural processing cen-<br /> ters and problem solving capabilities similar to sponge<br /> computers (p. 29). Although sponge computers are likely to<br /> be more generally useful, fungal versions may find use in<br /> applications where other fungal properties are desirable.<br /> They can grow almost anywhere there is sufficient mois-<br /> ture and organic material, and can be combined with a<br /> surveillance role, for example. <br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-06T21:11:06-08:00","id":1525149,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1524318-why-is-vtm-so-allergic-to-a-character-being-an-inventor-visonary?p=1525148#post1525148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Sponge Computers (TL10)<br /> Sponges have a homogeneous macroscopic structure<br /> suitable for hosting neural networks, but the natural ani-<br /> mals do not take advantage of this to perform complex<br /> thinking.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's quite the unreasonable jump. If sponges started hosting complex neural structures and sacrificed their spicules in the wild, they'd get eaten into extinction, because they wouldn't be made out of inedible glass anymore.<br /> <br /> (It's also entirely possible that fungi, specifically slime molds, might have some problem solving tricks of their own that should be understood before any attempt to hack in vertebrate neurons would be made. Science marches on!)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-06T21:28:12-08:00","id":1525150,"title":"","content":"And now, 2 examples from Ultra Tech.<br /> <br /> And no, I'm not taking the fancy exoskeleton suits, nor the laser beams or any such obvious choices.<br /> <br /> Instead, I picked some curious ones. The first, an Ultra Tech item for camping and/or outdoor survival:<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> <br /> Filtration Canteen (TL9)<br /> This canteen holds a quart of water. It removes impuri-<br /> ties, salts, microbes, and poisons. It can filter salt water, but<br /> not raw sewage or toxic waste. On its own, it adds a +1<br /> (quality) bonus to Survival skill when living off the land; it\u2019s<br /> also included in survival kits.<br /> One quart can be purified in 30 minutes (TL9), 10 min-<br /> utes (TL10), three minutes (TL11) or instantly (TL12). The<br /> filter must be replaced every 100 quarts at TL9, or 1,000<br /> quarts at TL10; a color change signals when it\u2019s time to<br /> change. An \u201cexhausted\u201d filter still has a few quarts of capac-<br /> ity, but only the GM knows how many. At TL11-12, the<br /> filter is permanent.<br /> The canteen is $180, 1 lb. (empty) or 3 lbs. (full). LC4.\u200b<br /> <br /> <br /> Now, a small tool for thieves and infiltrators:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Variable Lockpick (TL10) A memory-metal lockpick with a small imaging radar,<br /> an ultrasound imager, and its own contact mike. It recon-<br /> figures its shape into one of several hundred alternative<br /> forms after performing a sensor analysis of the lock. It<br /> includes a fiber-optic scope. Gives +4 to Lockpicking skill to<br /> open mechanical locks. It fits in a wallet., $50, neg., A/12 hr.<br /> LC2.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> And a little something for law enforcement:<br /> <br /> <br /> Neural Pacifier (TL10)<br /> Used legally by police, prison guards and hospitals, this<br /> restraint band projects a soothing hypnagogic field into the<br /> wearer\u2019s brain, keeping him sedated and compliant without<br /> risking drugs or injury.<br /> The neural pacifier has two settings: sleep and control.<br /> On \u201csleep,\u201d it places the wearer into a deep slumber. He<br /> cannot be awakened until the device is removed or turned<br /> off. On \u201ccontrol,\u201d the headband projects frequencies that<br /> allow the user to retain consciousness while suppressing<br /> aggressive tendencies, making the subject easily led. It<br /> effectively gives him the Slave Mentality disadvantage.<br /> The device can be resisted. After it is activated, the wear-<br /> er gets a roll against the higher of HT-3 or Will-3 each sec-<br /> ond to avoid succumbing to the effects. Once a roll is failed,<br /> the effects persist for as long as the device remains on.<br /> $500, 0.25 lbs., B/100 hr. LC3. This option can also be built<br /> into sensory restraints (above).<br /> <br /> <br /> So, as you guys can see, it covers pretty much every aspects of life. Yes yes, the book also have &quot;da guns&quot;. But it has so much more. It covers the future techs for media, education, crime and law enforcement, day to day life, medicine and much much more<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-06T21:48:25-08:00","id":1525153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1524318-why-is-vtm-so-allergic-to-a-character-being-an-inventor-visonary?p=1525149#post1525149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's quite the unreasonable jump. If sponges started hosting complex neural structures and sacrificed their spicules in the wild, they'd get eaten into extinction, because they wouldn't be made out of inedible glass anymore.<br /> <br /> (It's also entirely possible that fungi, specifically slime molds, might have some problem solving tricks of their own that should be understood before any attempt to hack in vertebrate neurons would be made. Science marches on!)</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, that's why those highly complex things are TL 10.<br /> <br /> Just for clarification, TL 9 will (would?) be when we are using nanobots on our daily lives. TL 10 is more or less &quot;ALL HAIL THE MACHINE LORD!&quot;. Some Techs of TL 10 include self replicating factories that can terraform entire planets in a matter of months.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, TL 11 is the pinnacle of any SciFi possibility, it's the truly outlandish stuff, because TL 12 is more like Fantasy than SciFi; TL 12 is basically magic <br /> <br /> Thus, when the book says that Sponge Computers or Neural Fungi are TL 10, it truly is because those are really wondrous stuff from crazy futuristic aliens.<br /> <br /> So, to answer your question... Undoubtedly, those &quot;Sponge Brains&quot; would be engineered (grown?) to repel predators.<br /> <br /> Or, maybe, would they actually be &quot;smart organic glass&quot;?<br /> <br /> Notice that most of those wouldn't be grown into the open ocean, although a TL 11 super sponge computer could be grown to encompass the entire world (or worlds). But then, TL 11 is TRULY insane. If you read on the book the stuff that TL 11 can do, it is truly ludicrous - as it should be.<br /> <br /> Most of those sponge computers would be used as... Computers. With the advantage that, rather than requiring a factory to manufacture, you just need a tube (acting as a &quot;vatbrain&quot;), nutrients and a sample of the sponge.<br /> <br /> Or the weaponized version that works as a &quot;brain parasite&quot;, growing inside the head and replacing the brain of an individual.<br /> <br /> But yeah, a super sponge computer encompassing an entire world would be possible at TL 11. Maybe every colony on oceanic worlds begin with one <br /> <br /> And at TL 12 you could do really silly things like &quot;intelligent electromagnetic waves&quot; that live inside stars (and no, this is a SciFi idea actually), or you could make living metal and such.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-07T09:43:29-08:00","id":1525168,"title":"","content":"I know how TLs work, GURPS was my third rpg. I was more taking exception to the futurist tone that it used, especially since we're discovering new things about slime mold problem solving years after the book was written. Any given sci-fi setting will often suffer from Science Marching On, though some took an intentional dive into it in the first place (BattleTech and OGRE both assume bonkers advances in materials engineering for armor that are heavily a Clarke's Law magical grade of bullshit, for example).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-07T10:04:06-08:00","id":1525169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1524318-why-is-vtm-so-allergic-to-a-character-being-an-inventor-visonary?p=1525168#post1525168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know how TLs work, GURPS was my third rpg. I was more taking exception to the futurist tone that it used, especially since we're discovering new things about slime mold problem solving years after the book was written. Any given sci-fi setting will often suffer from Science Marching On, though some took an intentional dive into it in the first place (BattleTech and OGRE both assume bonkers advances in materials engineering for armor that are heavily a Clarke's Law magical grade of bullshit, for example).</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep. Somethings there are outdated, some were already reached (!!!) and some are no longer feasible, but it's still a good source. I use it as my technomamcers toolbox of toys for my Technocrats and the Traditional techies, it's very cool.<br /> <br /> Nevertheless, just imagine a huge sponge computer covering the entire bottle of the oceans, how cool of a concept is that","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-07T10:58:17-08:00","id":1525173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1524318-why-is-vtm-so-allergic-to-a-character-being-an-inventor-visonary?p=1525169#post1525169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yep. Somethings there are outdated, some were already reached (!!!) and some are no longer feasible, but it's still a good source. I use it as my technomamcers toolbox of toys for my Technocrats and the Traditional techies, it's very cool.<br /> <br /> Nevertheless, just imagine a huge sponge computer covering the entire bottle of the oceans, how cool of a concept is that</div> </div> </div> </div>You'd need someone to clean them frequently due to marine snow (read: what would be dust and detritus on dry land), and microbes would be a constant worry - either new ones looking to get in and munch on the neural matter, or whatever humanity flushes into the oceans happening upon a new food source.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}